          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 4: Step-by-Step Instructions -->
      <h2>How to Resize Photos &amp; Signatures for CAT in 4 Easy Steps</h2>
      <div class="steps-list">
        <div class="step-card">
          <div class="step-number">1</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h4>Select Your CAT Category</h4>
            <p>Select <strong>General CAT</strong>, <strong>IIM PGP / MBA Entrance</strong>, or <strong>Non-IIM Associate Institutes</strong> from the dropdown. Keep <em>General CAT</em> for universal official compliance.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step-card">
          <div class="step-number">2</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h4>Select Document Type (Photo or Signature)</h4>
            <p>Toggle between the <strong>Photograph</strong> and <strong>Signature</strong> tabs. The Active Target Specifications immediately display the verified dimension and file size thresholds.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step-card">
          <div class="step-number">3</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h4>Upload Your Image</h4>
            <p>Drop any JPG, PNG, or WebP file into the dropzone. The client-side engine automatically scales the image, whitens the background, and compresses the file into the exact allowed byte range (max 80 KB).</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step-card">
          <div class="step-number">4</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h4>Inspect Checklist &amp; Download</h4>
            <p>Verify that all four official portal checks (Dimensions, File Size, Format, and Background) display <strong>PASS</strong>. Click <strong>Download Compliant File</strong> to save your application-ready JPG.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 5: Common Rejection Causes -->
      <h2>Common Reasons for Image Rejection on the IIM CAT Portal</h2>
      <ul class="rejection-list">
        <li><strong>File Size Exceeding 80 KB:</strong> The iimcat.ac.in portal enforces a strict binary upload ceiling of 80.0 KB. Any file of 81 KB or greater fails with an immediate portal error.</li>
        <li><strong>Signatures in Capital / Block Letters:</strong> Submitting a signature written entirely in uppercase letters or initials is strictly prohibited. Always sign in continuous cursive running script.</li>
        <li><strong>Colored or Dark Backgrounds:</strong> Backgrounds featuring blue curtains, household walls, or outdoor foliage are strictly rejected. Only pure white backgrounds (#FFFFFF) pass validation.</li>
        <li><strong>Low Resolution under 150 DPI:</strong> Blurry or pixelated scans that look smudged fail identity scrutiny. Our engine ensures crisp reproduction with 150+ DPI calibration.</li>
        <li><strong>Wearing Caps, Hats, or Dark Glasses:</strong> Headgear (except religious attire like Sikh turbans) and tinted spectacles are forbidden. Eyes, ears, and facial contours must be fully visible.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- Section 6: Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) -->
      <div class="faq-container">
        <div class="faq-header">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (CAT Photo &amp; Signature Specs)</h2>
          <p>Get quick, verified answers to common candidate questions regarding IIM CAT application image uploads.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-grid">
          {faqItems.map((item) => (
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">
                <span>{item.q}</span>
                <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                  <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>{item.a}</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

